@prefix asref: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> skos:scopeNote "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations."@en .
asref:CRSShape rdfs:label "CRSShape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of asref:CoordinateReferenceSystem; objects of asref:groundControlPointCRS, asref:hasCRS. A coordinate reference system is a resource (an IRI or a blank node), not a literal. Each focus node is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). asref:coordinateEpoch takes at most one value; each is an xsd:decimal literal. asref:crsIdentifier takes at most one value; each is an IRI. asref:wktString takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal at least 1 character long."@en .
asref:CoefficientVectorShape rdfs:label "Coefficient Vector Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. A coefficient vector is an RDF list (an IRI or a blank node), not a literal. A conforming value is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). Each member of the list is a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). A coefficient vector must be a well-formed finite RDF list of exactly 20 cells."@en .
asref:CoordinateReferenceSystem skos:definition "A resource describing the coordinate system and reference frame in which spatial coordinates are interpreted."@en .
asref:CubicRationalTransformShape rdfs:label "Cubic Rational Transform Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of asref:CubicRationalTransform; objects of asref:hasRationalTransform. A cubic rational transform is a resource (an IRI or a blank node), not a literal. Each focus node is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). asref:heightOffset takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:heightScale takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite) greater than 0. asref:latitudeOffset takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:latitudeScale takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite) greater than 0. asref:lineDenominator takes exactly one value, a value conforming to asref:CoefficientVectorShape. asref:lineNumerator takes exactly one value, a value conforming to asref:CoefficientVectorShape. asref:lineOffset takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:lineScale takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite) greater than 0. asref:longitudeOffset takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:longitudeScale takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite) greater than 0. asref:polynomialBasis takes exactly one value, an IRI. asref:sampleDenominator takes exactly one value, a value conforming to asref:CoefficientVectorShape. asref:sampleNumerator takes exactly one value, a value conforming to asref:CoefficientVectorShape. asref:sampleOffset takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:sampleScale takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite) greater than 0."@en .
asref:FiniteDoubleShape rdfs:label "Finite Double Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. A finite number is an xsd:double or xsd:float literal that is not NaN or infinite. A conforming value is an xsd:double or xsd:float literal that is finite (not NaN or infinite)."@en .
asref:FloatValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. A float value is an xsd:double or xsd:float literal. A conforming value is an xsd:double or xsd:float literal."@en .
asref:GeoTransformShape rdfs:label "Geo Transform Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of asref:GeoTransform; objects of asref:hasGeoTransform. A geotransform is a resource (an IRI or a blank node), not a literal. Each focus node is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). asref:originX takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:originY takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:scaleX takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:scaleY takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:skewX takes at most one value; each is a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:skewY takes at most one value; each is a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite)."@en .
asref:GroundControlPointShape rdfs:label "Ground Control Point Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of asref:GroundControlPoint; objects of asref:hasGroundControlPoint. asref:gcpIdentifier takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal. asref:gcpPixelX takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:gcpPixelY takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:gcpX takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:gcpY takes exactly one value, a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite). asref:gcpZ takes at most one value; each is a finite number (an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, not NaN or infinite)."@en .
asref:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
asref:PixelCenter skos:definition "Registration of a cell's value at the centre of its cell (a point sample, such as an elevation post). It does not move the grid: the normalized affine stays corner-based, and a source whose native transform is centre-based is shifted by half a cell when it is normalized, once, at lifting time."@en .
asref:PixelCorner skos:definition "Registration of a cell's value at, or as an area from, the cell's upper-left corner. The normalized affine is corner-based whatever the registration: column/row (0, 0) is the outer corner of the first cell."@en .
asref:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using asref:coordinateEpoch, asref:epsgCode, asref:footprintWKT, asref:gcpIdentifier, asref:gcpPixelX, asref:gcpPixelY, asref:gcpX, asref:gcpY, asref:gcpZ, asref:heightOffset, asref:heightScale, asref:latitudeOffset, asref:latitudeScale, asref:lineOffset, asref:lineScale, asref:longitudeOffset, asref:longitudeScale, asref:originLatitude, asref:originLongitude, asref:originX, asref:originY, asref:sampleOffset, asref:sampleScale, asref:scaleX, asref:scaleY, asref:skewX, asref:skewY. asref:coordinateEpoch takes an xsd:decimal literal (rdfs:range xsd:decimal). asref:epsgCode takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). asref:footprintWKT takes a geosparql:wktLiteral or xsd:string literal (rdfs:range: their union). asref:gcpIdentifier takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). asref:gcpPixelX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:gcpPixelY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:gcpX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:gcpY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:gcpZ takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:heightOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:heightScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:latitudeOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:latitudeScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:lineOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:lineScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:longitudeOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:longitudeScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:originLatitude takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:originLongitude takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:originX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:originY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:sampleOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:sampleScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:scaleX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:scaleY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:skewX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float). asref:skewY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double or xsd:float)."@en .
asref:epsgCode skos:definition "The positive numeric code identifying a coordinate reference system in the EPSG registry; it is not a complete substitute for all CRS metadata."@en .
asref:gcpIdentifier skos:definition "The source-local identifier distinguishing a control point within its control-point set."@en .
asref:gcpX skos:definition "The first ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
asref:gcpY skos:definition "The second ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
asref:hasGeoTransform skos:definition "The complete affine transformation resource relating grid column/row coordinates to ground coordinates."@en .
asref:hasGroundControlPoint skos:definition "A measured or supplied correspondence between an image-grid location and a ground coordinate."@en .
asref:hasRationalTransform skos:definition "The rational-polynomial geolocation model associated with a resource, with its basis contract declared explicitly."@en .
asref:pixelRegistration skos:definition "Where a cell's value is located within the cell: at its centre (asref:PixelCenter, a point sample) or representing the cell from its upper-left corner (asref:PixelCorner, an area value). It describes the value, not the grid: the normalized affine (asref:GeoTransform) is always corner-based, so this property never shifts the affine or the column and row of a world point."@en .
